    "created_at": "2019-10-11T20:28:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-11T20:28:21Z",
    "body": "An+B is great for selecting the Nth element, or every Nth element. It *can* be used to select every element before/after a certain N, but it's not very intuitive. I'd much rather use comparison operators like MQs allow.\r\n\r\n(I don't think the `2n` use-case is needed in headings, so the loss of functionality doesn't seem significant.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
