    "created_at": "2019-10-12T17:53:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-12T17:53:13Z",
    "body": "As I commented in the related CSS issue discussion, there is open discussion (https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/4140) about adding an intuitive range syntax to the CSS nth-child selectors. If both that and this proposal are adopted, then it would make sense to harmonize the syntax. There might not be much use case for `:heading(odd)` selector, but it would be simpler for authors and implementers if the bits inside the `:heading(numeric selector)` and `:nth-child(numeric selector)` are parsed the same.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
